{
  "about": [
    "The parity table between openplate.de and the openplate app (M263 specs 01 and 04).",
    "Each expected value was produced by running the app functions once: computeBmrKcal, computeTdeeKcal and suggestDailyKcal in app/models/body-metrics.ts, computeReferenceProteinFloor with the dge basis for the reference protein, and applyEatingStyle with the high-protein style for the high protein figure.",
    "The same file lives in both repositories, byte for byte. Each repository tests its own functions against it, so a constant changed on one side fails that side.",
    "The app takes a birth year, so its test passes birthYear = currentYear - ageYears. A null expected value means the calculator gives no answer for that input.",
    "A row marked appOnly carries an input the site does not ask for, such as a pregnancy trimester. Only the app runs it."
  ],
